---
import ContentLayout from '@/layouts/ContentLayout.astro';
---

<ContentLayout
  title="Shipping & duties · all included"
  description="Every price includes insured express shipping to any US address and all import duties and tariffs. Delivery in 5–10 business days with tracking."
  h1="Shipping &amp; duties"
  intro="The price on the page is the price at your door."
  updated="2026-09-28"
  toc={[
    { id: 'included', label: 'What’s included' },
    { id: 'times', label: 'Delivery times' },
    { id: 'tariffs', label: 'Tariffs, honestly' },
    { id: 'delivery', label: 'On delivery day' },
  ]}
>
  <section id="included" class="scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>What’s included</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Insured express courier shipping from Turkey to any address in the 50 US states.</li>
      <li>
        All US import duties, tariffs, merchandise processing fees, and customs brokerage. Shipments
        are sent Delivered Duty Paid.
      </li>
      <li>Tracking by email the moment it ships, and a text if you want one.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Not included: sales tax, which Stripe calculates at checkout where required by your state.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="times" class="scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>Delivery times</h2>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Size</th>
          <th>Ships within</th>
          <th>Arrives in</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Up to 6×9</td>
          <td>2 business days</td>
          <td>5–8 business days</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>8×10 and 9×12</td>
          <td>2 business days</td>
          <td>6–10 business days</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>10×14 and up</td>
          <td>3 business days</td>
          <td>7–12 business days</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>
      Each product page shows the note for that specific rug. Holidays in Turkey (Eid, Republic Day)
      can add a day or two; I’ll tell you if they will.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="tariffs" class="scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>Tariffs, honestly</h2>
    <p>
      US tariff policy on Turkish goods has changed several times recently. Whatever it is on the
      day your rug clears customs, I pay it. If a rug is already sold to you and a tariff goes up
      before it ships, that’s my cost, not yours. [EDIT: keep this paragraph current with the
      Section 301 status.]
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="delivery" class="scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>On delivery day</h2>
    <p>
      Rugs ship rolled in a heavy bag inside a box or sleeve. Check the outside for damage before
      signing if you can. Unroll it, let it lie flat for a day, and vacuum once (no beater bar). Any
      shipping damage: photos within 48 hours and I’ll handle the claim; you won’t.
    </p>
  </section>
</ContentLayout>
